    "price_impact_note": "Reserves moved DEUS 19,303,121 -> 19,393,771 and VIRTUAL 515,912 -> 513,501, i.e. the mark fell 0.933% in that one block. So a single vesting recipient can move this pool by ~1% with a 91.5k dump - the book absorbs ~$1.7k of notional per 1% of price. That is the number that matters for the operator's $0.012 / $0.041 triggers: a 34% move down to $0.012 would require ~2.5M DEUS of selling at constant liquidity, i.e. 7 days of the entire claim drip dumped at market in one go. The $0.012 gate is therefore NOT reachable by routine emissions - it needs a deliberate large seller.",
