    "impact_note": "TWO numbers, do not conflate them. (a) The POOL MARK fell 0.02769675 -> 0.02714852 VIRTUAL per DEUS = -1.979%, measured straight off the reserves (DEUS 18,961,647.3772 -> 19,152,146.2397, VIRTUAL 525,176.0739 -> 519,952.3541) at blocks 0x328cee6 -> 0x328cee7. This is the true depth cost. (b) The PRINTED USD tape went $0.0179585 -> $0.0171738 = -4.37%, but that gap is inflated by VIRTUAL itself moving and by the stale prior print. Use (a) for depth math. RECALIBRATION: 319,562 DEUS cost the pool 1.98%, i.e. ~$2.9k of notional per 1% of price - NOT the ~$1.7k/1% inferred from the 91.5k dump on 2026-10-23. The book is deeper than the earlier estimate. A RECORD-SIZED unstake does not collapse this pool.",
    "absorbed_in_block": "The dump did NOT sit on the book. SIX buys printed in the SAME block 0x328cee7 (53006055) totalling 125,867.74 DEUS ($1,771), led by 0x6011b76b (62,825 DEUS / $1,093) and 0x6abea499 (29,739 DEUS / $514); a seventh buy of 11,529.69 DEUS ($201) landed in the very next block (0x328ceee). Same-block + next-block absorption = 137,397.44 DEUS. Net DEUS left in the pool after the event = 319,562.23 - 137,397.44 - 3,195.62 (fee to 0x205db642) = 178,969.17. That same-block bid is why -1.98% did not become a -10% cascade.",
    "remaining_position": "CRITICAL FORWARD SIGNAL: this wallet STILL HOLDS one more xDEUS NFT - tokenId 1396 (0x574), confirmed via tokenOfOwnerByIndex(owner, 0) on 0xe6d5f743. Note 1396 < 1492, so it was staked BEFORE the one it just burned: this is a multi-position staker unwinding in tranches, earliest first or by size, not a one-off. Size of #1396 NOT yet measured (escrow has no public per-token getter that resolved; do not assume it matches 319,562). Watch this address and the escrow Burn event for tokenId 1396 - that is the trigger for the next dump.",
    "read": "This is the first time the 5-day xDEUS cooldown has actually been PAID and then converted to market selling in the observable record. It validates the STRATEGY premise: the cooldown is the real cost of the multiplier, and someone did pay it to exit. It is NOT routine CLAIM emission - the DEUS came out of escrow, via an NFT burn, not from the 0x5cbf vesting vault. So this is existing staked float leaving, not new supply.",
    "observed_at": "2026-10-24T05:08:55Z",
    "price_impact_method": "pool-reserve constant-product mark: VIRTUAL/DEUS 0.02769675 -> 0.02714852 = -1.979%",
    "exec_price_usd": 0.0171737950710244,
    "prior_print_usd": 0.0179584527229686,
    "distance_math": "Constant product, price = k/D^2, so reaching $0.012 from $0.01809 needs D -> D*sqrt(0.01809/0.012) = D*1.2278, i.e. ~4.36M DEUS of NET pool inflow with zero offsetting bids. That is 13.6x this record dump, or 15.4 days of the ENTIRE CLAIM drip (283,140/day) sold at market in one go. The $0.012 gate remains a deliberate-whale event, not an emission drift.",
    "xdeus_supply_note": "xDEUS totalSupply 0x18160ddd: 1724 at -24h (0x3284782) -> 1727 pre-burn (0x328c61b) -> 1726 immediately post-burn (0x328c61c, the NFT #1492 burn removed exactly 1) -> 1727 now (0x328f042). So one NEW xDEUS position was minted shortly after this burn. Net 24h change is +3 NFTs, i.e. staking is still net ADDITIVE despite the record exit. Do not describe this event as an exodus."
  },
