  "arbitrage_note_1502z": {
    "observed_at": "2026-10-24T15:02:41Z",
    "what": "CRITICAL ATTRIBUTION FINDING. The 30 'buys' in the 1h window are mostly NOT directional buying — they are two-leg arbitrage between the deepest pool and the three USDC V3 pools, plus triangular routing.",
    "evidence": "In the DEUS Transfer legs of each swap tx, the DEUS leaves the deepest pool and lands in an intermediate CONTRACT (0xae629bf1cf17cbdd1b8e9a462519f678d8b40b3f, 0xb88bb63113b50ff258138d8349e8521e2bf43654, 0x29be31e7ef434a74d69da1cb6b51ad65c83e9a7b, 0x4623be8e66e455b6954dd46149a0585dddbc6c87, 0x498581ff718922c3f8e6a244956af099b2652b2b) and then is forwarded IN THE SAME TX to a USDC V3 pool (0x58dba34e, 0x1b2f3f5c, 0x75bc1495) or to the 1inch v6 router 0x111111125421ca6dc452d289314280a0f8842a65. The paying sender (tx.from) is a distinct EOA each time, but the DEUS never rests in an EOA balance — it is pass-through.",
    "why_it_matters": "TELL 19 said absorption is conditional on a bid being present. This refines it: the bid can be STRUCTURAL (arb) rather than directional. Arb bids are self-limiting — they close the moment the deepest pool's mark converges to the USDC venues' mark. They do NOT represent new money accumulating DEUS.",
    "quantification": "The deepest pool sat at $0.01723 while the USDC V3 median was $0.01730217 (-0.42% discount). That persistent discount is exactly what the arb flow was harvesting. As the deepest pool reprices upward, the arb stops.",
    "counter_evidence": "NOT ALL of it is arb. tx 0x7fa7d784 (blk 53031032) sent 5,502.35 DEUS from the pool to 0xeb7c90d3d8eb5cce9c3da4725ba9d5177cf8cc50 with no forwarding leg in the same tx, and 0xf96f9b46 at blk 53031706 routed 5,842.91 DEUS through sink 0x939e398d2c31b0757d009222de99c6e461d3de15 to EOA 0x49a782c2 — a held position, not arb."
  },
